Novaras was under siege. Ghouls wearing stolen faces attacked from inside the walls while Demorai forces battered the gates.
Krill's sister fought among the invaders. The party defended the streets, but Renia saw Zanarak on the wall and abandoned the civilians to pursue him.
Vera: Krill's sister is still here. We need everyone.
Renia: Zanarak is the reason any of this is happening.
Karak followed Renia into the crush of ghouls. The rest of the party fought to protect the city.
[wait_input]
Moka, Vera, and Krill drove Krill's sister back, but she pleaded with her brother and escaped once more.
Karak and Renia defeated a dark knight too late to reach Zanarak. The enemy had already vanished.
Renia: If I had the rest of the armor, I could have stopped him.
The city survived. Krill mourned another escape. Moka and Vera no longer trusted Renia's priorities.
[wait_input]
On the road west, the party met Nami Mitsune, a katai traveler heading toward her home in Wei.
Nami: I can pay for an escort. And I have questions for Karak.
Renia watched Nami flirt with Karak, unsettled by how easily she drew his attention.
The group bickered through the journey. Nami cooked a meal and invited them to tell funny stories. Their laughter gave way to silence when Renia joked about a night she could not remember.
[wait_input]
The party found a village under Demorai attack and stayed to help defend it. Karak and Renia fought beside the villagers, while Vera urged Renia to remember the people behind her plans.
An elder asked Vera whether she feared loving Karak because she might one day lose him. Vera had no answer.
In the forest, the party met the living tree that guarded the gauntlets. It gave Renia the armor piece after Grim argued that people could grow into the power they sought.
The gauntlets made Renia faster. The armor's whispers urged her to feed it souls.
[wait_input]
Vera received word that her mother would be tried for dark magecraft. The party turned toward Newyark despite Renia's objections.
Karak: We cannot abandon her mother to save a few days.
Renia: You always choose everyone else.
At Newyark, Erik of House Castormore secured their release from the Inquisition. Vera visited her mother, who admitted she had worked with a dark mage to protect Vera.
The mage was found dead in his cell. In the cellar of Vera's childhood home, the party discovered the remains of an unfinished spirit ritual.
[wait_input]
Vera revealed she had once served as an inquisitor and knew the ritual was not what the investigators claimed. Before they could prove it, the party had to flee through abandoned mines with Vera's mother.
Celeste and the Red Arrows ambushed them underground. The party barely escaped, and Moka was gravely injured.
Karak traveled with Nami to Tenyrue and met his uncle. He learned his mother had died stopping a cult, and an old god had bound Grim to him as an infant.
Grim: I knew. I am not your friend in the way you hoped.
Karak: Then I will decide who I am without you deciding for me.
[wait_input]
Nami offered Karak a place in her family and a chance to build a life beyond Renia's vow. Karak returned to his companions, still unsure what he wanted.
The party reunited in the mountains. Renia trained through her injuries, convinced the armor was the only way to become strong enough.
Celeste's warning lingered: more armor would not make Renia invincible.
Krill and Moka considered leaving, but stayed because they could not abandon Karak.
[wait_input]
The party crossed the mountains toward Tenyrue. A ghostly caravan emerged in the fog and offered cursed relics that promised to fulfill their desires.
Grim warned them not to touch anything. Krill secretly took an amulet; it glowed with visions of her sister and a possible path to resurrection.
Nami guided Karak to his uncle, who explained how Karak's mother died stopping a cult and how an old god had bound Grim to him as an infant.
Nami offered Karak a place in her family and a life beyond Renia's vow. Karak returned to the party, but the choice stayed with him.
[wait_input]
The party helped defend a village from Demorai raiders. Renia wanted to continue toward the armor; Vera and Karak insisted the villagers needed them.
They fought through the night and saved the settlement. An elder encouraged Vera to stop treating her love for Karak as a reason to avoid him.
Renia's nightmares worsened. The blades promised that if she fed them enough souls, she could become powerful enough to defeat Zanarak.
