The party followed a map to the Orasomore islands, where a sunken temple held another armor piece. In the fog, they fought strange creatures and found shelter with a woman who protected her home with old symbols.
The temple guardians mirrored each traveler and demanded their darkest truths. Renia confessed to Nami's murder.
Karak: I trusted you with my life.
Renia: I can still make this right. You will understand.
Krill found the cuirass and begged Renia to stop. She killed Krill in the struggle, then put on the armor and fled.
[wait_input]
Moka left the party to mourn Krill. Vera asked Karak to leave with her.
Vera: We can still choose a life that belongs to us.
Karak: We have to stop Renia before the armor takes anyone else.
Vera stayed beside him. Together, they followed Renia's trail.
[wait_input]
Celeste confronted Renia and defeated her. Renia escaped, determined to find the last piece: the helmet beneath the black sea.
The helmet transformed Renia into a demonic figure. At the same time, Karak and Vera admitted their feelings and chose to face the future together.
Hanlar traveled to Gerano with Celeste, believing he could claim the armor. Celeste planned only to watch what happened.
[wait_input]
[wait_input]
Gerano had become a prison under Demorai occupation. Renia arrived and tore through the enemy ranks, declaring that she had returned to save her people.
The survivors recoiled from her monstrous appearance. The armor demanded souls to sustain her.
Renia: Give me your strength, and I will protect you!
They fled. Renia fed on those who would not surrender their lives, convinced she was saving the city.
[wait_input]
Karak and Vera confronted her.
Karak: This isn't the promise we made. You are killing the people you came to save.
Renia: I can fix everything when I have enough power.
The storm announced Zanarak's arrival. Renia had to choose between the life-force of Gerano and the enemy she had pursued for years.
Hanlar arrived with guards. Celeste watched from a hill as Renia killed him, ending the threat he had posed to her family.
[wait_input]
Zanarak arrived without recognizing Renia. A servant spoke for him.
Servant: Lord Zanarak has heard speeches like this a thousand times. To him, the end of a city is only another day.
Renia attacked in fury, draining the dying to keep fighting. Vera was wounded. Karak spent Grim's bargains to shield civilians and get Vera out of danger.
Karak: Renia, come with us. We can leave this behind.
Renia: I have come too far. I need everything.
